      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled daily dose of ibuprofen. The usual adult maximum is 3,200 mg/day for prescription use, given as no more than 800 mg per dose. A dose this high raises the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nWas this a typo? Some possible intended orders:\n- **800 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the usual maximum for inflammatory conditions or severe pain\n- **400\u2013600 mg by mouth, every 6 hours**, a typical dose for mild to moderate pain\n- **1600 mg total per day**, divided into smaller doses\n\nIf you do want the order as written, tell me the clinical reason and I'll enter it with a note. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
